1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:02,529
Ten infamous crime bosses.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,756
From Capone to El Mayo.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,269
One of them was brought
down by a tax bill.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,200
Another built a prison for himself.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,747
The last one got life in July 2026.

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:17,929
Ten bosses.

7
00:00:18,099 --> 00:00:19,814
100 years of history.

8
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,651
Al Capone was born in Brooklyn in 1899.

9
00:00:24,821 --> 00:00:29,877
In 1919 he moved to Chicago, and a few
years later he was its crime boss.

10
00:00:30,127 --> 00:00:32,955
He took over when Johnny
Torrio retired to Italy.

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:38,405
Prohibition made him rich:
an estimated 100 million dollars.

12
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:44,535
Chicago officials named him
Public Enemy Number One in 1930.

13
00:00:44,705 --> 00:00:48,495
Many linked him to the violence,
but nothing was proven in court.

14
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,329
Taxes caught him: 11
years in prison, in 1931.

15
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:00,173
He ended up in Alcatraz,
and was freed in 1939, seriously ill.

16
00:01:00,343 --> 00:01:02,997
He died in Florida in 1947.

17
00:01:03,247 --> 00:01:06,935
He spent his last years
as a recluse, at his Palm Island home.

18
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:12,112
Born Salvatore Lucania
in Sicily, he grew up in New York.

19
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,217
In 1931, during a mob war,

20
00:01:16,237 --> 00:01:20,669
he secretly switched sides
and helped bring down a rival boss.

21
00:01:20,919 --> 00:01:22,963
That rival boss was Joe Masseria.

22
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,700
He then helped create the Commission,
a national governing board.

23
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:29,401
No more boss of bosses.

24
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,431
In 1936 he got 30 to 50 years.

25
00:01:33,601 --> 00:01:36,059
Ten years later, he was deported to Italy.

26
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:41,943
He died of a heart attack
at the Naples airport in 1962,

27
00:01:41,963 --> 00:01:45,576
while meeting a film producer
about a movie on his life.

28
00:01:45,826 --> 00:01:49,739
A legendary mob summit in Havana
was reportedly his idea.

29
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,901
Meyer Lansky, the mob's numbers man,

30
00:01:53,921 --> 00:01:57,613
was born in Grodno, in what
is now Belarus, in 1902.

31
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:01,978
A close ally of Luciano,

32
00:02:01,998 --> 00:02:06,044
he built gambling networks
in Florida, Havana and Las Vegas.

33
00:02:06,294 --> 00:02:08,238
He reportedly bribed Batista.

34
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:13,537
In 1970, facing a possible
tax case, he fled to Israel.

35
00:02:13,707 --> 00:02:17,783
Israel sent him back, and he was never
convicted of a major crime.

36
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:22,335
His only jail time was two
months, for gambling, in 1953.

37
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:26,426
Estimated holdings: 300 million dollars.

38
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:32,329
Yet one report says his estate
was only about 57,000.

39
00:02:32,499 --> 00:02:34,807
That figure comes from a single source.

40
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:41,774
John Gotti, born in the Bronx
in 1940, ran the Gambino family.

41
00:02:41,944 --> 00:02:45,362
In December 1985, boss
Paul Castellano was killed

42
00:02:45,382 --> 00:02:49,081
outside a Manhattan
steakhouse, and Gotti took over.

43
00:02:49,331 --> 00:02:51,229
He was nicknamed the Teflon Don.

44
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:56,952
Then his own underboss, Sammy
the Bull Gravano, turned on him.

45
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:05,389
In April 1992 he was convicted on 13
counts, and sentenced to life without parole.

46
00:03:05,639 --> 00:03:07,199
The sentence came that June.

47
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,824
He died of throat cancer in 2002.

48
00:03:11,074 --> 00:03:13,234
He was 61, in a prison hospital.

49
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:19,667
Totò Riina, born in Corleone, rose
to become Cosa Nostra's boss of bosses.

50
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:24,999
After more than 20 years on the run,
he was arrested in Palermo.

51
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:30,889
The Maxi Trial convicted
more than 300 mafiosi.

52
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:38,503
In 1992, bombs killed judges
Giovanni Falcone and Paolo Borsellino.

53
00:03:38,673 --> 00:03:43,530
Riina was convicted as the mastermind,
and Sicilians turned against the Mafia.

54
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:47,030
Police officers guarding
them also died in the attacks.

55
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,627
He died in prison in 2017.

56
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:58,228
Griselda Blanco, the Cocaine Godmother,
was born on Colombia's coast in 1943.

57
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,940
She reportedly smuggled
more than three tons

58
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:05,396
of cocaine a year into the United States.

59
00:04:05,566 --> 00:04:08,779
Her rivalries helped spark
Miami's Cocaine Cowboy wars.

60
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:16,362
She was arrested in 1985,
and deported to Colombia in 2004.

61
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:23,311
In 2012, at 69, she was shot
and killed in Medellín.

62
00:04:23,561 --> 00:04:26,887
Years earlier, she had named
her youngest son Michael Corleone.

63
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:34,219
Pablo Escobar, born in 1949,
helped found the Medellín Cartel.

64
00:04:34,469 --> 00:04:36,424
He was first arrested for car theft.

65
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:41,291
His fortune was estimated
at 25 to 30 billion dollars.

66
00:04:41,541 --> 00:04:43,665
Forbes listed him seven years in a row.

67
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:48,166
In 1982 he was elected
an alternate member of Congress,

68
00:04:48,186 --> 00:04:50,645
posing as a benefactor of the poor.

69
00:04:50,895 --> 00:04:53,320
His cartel dominated the cocaine trade.

70
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:59,956
In 1991 he surrendered, after a deal let
him build his own prison, La Catedral.

71
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:07,780
In December 1993, he died in a gunfight
with police on a Medellín rooftop.

72
00:05:08,030 --> 00:05:10,654
He had turned 44 just one day before.

73
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:15,633
His hippos still roam
Colombia, over 100 of them.

74
00:05:15,883 --> 00:05:17,559
Now an invasive species.

75
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:21,884
Matteo Messina Denaro, nicknamed Diabolik,

76
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:24,790
was born in Castelvetrano in 1962.

77
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:28,034
He was sentenced in absentia to life

78
00:05:28,054 --> 00:05:31,568
for the 1992 attacks
on Falcone and Borsellino.

79
00:05:31,818 --> 00:05:34,483
He was also convicted
of dozens of other killings.

80
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:39,401
After 30 years on the run,
he was arrested in January 2023,

81
00:05:39,421 --> 00:05:43,014
at a Palermo clinic where
he was treated for cancer.

82
00:05:43,264 --> 00:05:45,603
He used the false name Andrea Buonafede.

83
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:49,192
He died in September 2023, aged 61,

84
00:05:49,212 --> 00:05:52,798
closing the era
of the Godfather generation.

85
00:05:53,048 --> 00:05:55,025
Reports said he took his secrets with him.

86
00:05:56,400 --> 00:06:02,372
Joaquín Guzmán, El Chapo, was born
into poverty in Sinaloa in 1957.

87
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:08,339
American prosecutors say his Sinaloa
Cartel moved more than 1 million

88
00:06:08,359 --> 00:06:13,856
kilograms of drugs over 25 years, using
boats, submarines, planes and tunnels.

89
00:06:14,106 --> 00:06:16,003
He also paid millions in bribes.

90
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:21,578
In 2015 he escaped a Mexican
prison through a one-mile tunnel,

91
00:06:21,598 --> 00:06:25,642
with lighting, ventilation
and a small motorcycle on rails.

92
00:06:25,892 --> 00:06:28,999
Marines recaptured him in January 2016.

93
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:34,856
In 2019, an American court
sentenced him to life plus 30 years.

94
00:06:35,106 --> 00:06:37,634
He had been extradited in 2017.

95
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:42,178
He now sits at ADX Florence,
the Alcatraz of the Rockies.

96
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:49,862
Ismael El Mayo Zambada co-founded
the Sinaloa Cartel alongside El Chapo.

97
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:55,158
He stayed out
of the spotlight for decades,

98
00:06:55,178 --> 00:06:58,523
until July 2024, when
he was arrested near El Paso.

99
00:06:58,773 --> 00:07:01,017
El Chapo's son was arrested with him.

100
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:07,261
On July 20, 2026, a judge
sentenced him to life without parole,

101
00:07:07,281 --> 00:07:09,772
and a 15 billion dollar forfeiture.

102
00:07:09,942 --> 00:07:13,240
Prosecutors warned that loyalists
still run the cartel.

103
00:07:13,490 --> 00:07:16,232
He had pleaded guilty in August 2025.

104
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:21,055
Analysts say the cartel now faces
a fight over who takes charge.

105
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,192
Ten bosses.

106
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:29,327
Ten endings: taxes, betrayal,
a rooftop, a clinic, a cell.

107
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,831
Which of these ten shaped
organized crime the most?

